{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_orjwfffu7ekzwitrjgb3ndohq4wp2meuxpfxhf436rhweohzmhka","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01B1Tuca7jPMSFpFAqwgXuho","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport re\np='CONFIGS.md'; s=open(p).read()\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"**Consequence:** every configuration that reaches `compare_allocations`\n(rows for `compare_allocations`, `arity4`, `arity3`, `arity2`, `arity`)\nmust be compared with **process isolation**: one fresh subprocess loads\nonly the C `.so` and replays the whole call sequence, another fresh\nsubprocess loads only the Rust `.so` and replays the identical sequence,\nand the two stdout streams are compared byte-for-byte. This is a\n*stronger* test than in-process pairwise comparison because it also\npins the allocation *pattern* (number and order of malloc/free calls),\nnot just the returned integer.\n\nAllocator-independent entry points (`shift_array`, `process_string`,\n`apply_bitmask`, `init_matrix`) are compared in-process, pairwise.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**Consequence:** axis G is turned from nondeterministic noise into a\n*controlled input axis*. Immediately before every call that reaches\n`compare_allocations`, the harness normalizes the glibc tcache 32-byte\nbin:\n\n```rust\nlet a = malloc(4); let b = malloc(4);\nlet (lo, hi) = if a < b { (a, b) } else { (b, a) };\n// tcache is LIFO: the LAST pointer freed is handed back FIRST.\nif want_ascending { free(hi); free(lo); }   // -> ptr1 < ptr2, result 1\nelse              { free(lo); free(hi); }   // -> ptr1 > ptr2, result 2\n```\n\nVerified deterministic for both libraries and both arms:\n\n```\nasc=true   compare_allocations( 5,6) -> (C 11, Rust 11) x8\nasc=true   compare_allocations(-5,6) -> (C  1, Rust  1) x8\nasc=false  compare_allocations( 5,6) -> (C 12, Rust 12) x8\nasc=false  compare_allocations(-5,6) -> (C  2, Rust  2) x8\n```\n\nSo `asc` becomes an explicit configuration axis (`G=asc` / `G=desc`) and\n**both** pointer-ordering arms of `compare_allocations` are exercised\ndeliberately, in-process, pairwise. Rows below marked `norm` are run\nunder *both* `G=asc` and `G=desc`.\"\"\")\ns = s.replace(\"`iso` = process-isolated\\nbyte-for-byte stdout comparison. `pair` = in-process pairwise compare.\",\n\"`pair` = in-process pairwise\\ncompare. `norm` = in-process pairwise compare with the tcache normalized\\nbefore *every* call, run twice: once with `G=asc` and once with `G=desc`.\")\ns = s.replace('| iso |','| norm |')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ngrep -c '| norm |' CONFIGS.md","description":"Update CONFIGS.md with normalization methodology"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3352,"cache_read_input_tokens":53103,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3352,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1c4dd0b-13a9-41fa-b25b-7eb02d42a017","uuid":"24363dcc-0e87-4610-9cb8-d9e436e09e60","timestamp":"2026-09-05T13:00:26.155Z"}
