{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_hb5e7vlhswhn46n2dpjbwu5yf7yjfpll326obo3geql3narod5kq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_016VEYbRuiyp1Pr4A51Mikvf","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Refactor heap-sensitive test call sites","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Mechanical refactor task in the Rust crate at `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-a7i4Gw/translation`.\n\nDo NOT modify `tests/common/mod.rs`, `src/lib.rs`, `CONFIGS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `SYMBOLS.md`, or anything under `c_src/`.\n\nOnly edit these two files:\n- `tests/phase_b_valid.rs`\n- `tests/phase_c_errors.rs`\n\n## Context\n\n`tests/common/mod.rs` (already written, do not change) provides these helpers:\n\n```rust\npub fn normalize_heap(asc: bool);\npub const BOTH_ORDERS: [bool; 2] = [true, false];\n\n/// Serialized + retrying differential call. Returns the agreed C value,\n/// or panics with a divergence report if C and Rust disagree on all 8 attempts.\npub fn diff_norm(\n    row: &str,\n    ctx: impl std::fmt::Debug,\n    asc: bool,\n    cf: &mut dyn FnMut() -> c_int,\n    rf: &mut dyn FnMut() -> c_int,\n) -> c_int;\n\n/// Same but for a replayed SEQUENCE. Returns the agreed C vector or panics.\npub fn diff_norm_seq<T: PartialEq + std::fmt::Debug>(\n    row: &str,\n    asc: bool,\n    cf: &mut dyn FnMut() -> Vec<T>,\n    rf: &mut dyn FnMut() -> Vec<T>,\n) -> Vec<T>;\n\n#[track_caller] pub fn eq_i32(row: &str, ctx: impl Debug, c: c_int, r: c_int);\n#[track_caller] pub fn eq_slice(row: &str, ctx: impl Debug, c: &[c_int], r: &[c_int]);\n```\n\n## The transformation\n\nEverywhere in those two test files that currently follows this manual pattern:\n\n```rust\nnormalize_heap(asc);\nlet cv = unsafe { (c.SOMEFN)(args) };\nnormalize_heap(asc);\nlet rv = unsafe { (r.SOMEFN)(args) };\neq_i32(\"row-name\", ctx, cv, rv);\n```\n\nreplace it with:\n\n```rust\nlet cv = diff_norm(\"row-name\", ctx, asc,\n    &mut ||